  "purpose": "Preliminary rack-unit, PDU-outlet, switch-port, VLAN and power-feed proposal for the primary 42U rack. The v0.3 README lists rack-unit positions and outlet assignments as deliberately unresolved, so this document is a proposal for owner and commissioning review, not a decided elevation.",
  "review_required_before_use": true,
  "supersedes": null,
  "placement_principles": [
    "Heaviest items lowest: UPS at the bottom of the rack, then power distribution, then storage and compute.",
    "Switches and the router at the top so patching, uplinks and console access stay above the heat sources.",
    "Environmental monitoring high enough that inlet and exhaust sensor leads reach the full height of the rack.",
    "Contiguous free rack units kept in one block in the middle rather than scattered, so a future chassis fits.",
    "Zero-U, door-mounted and sensor-port-powered devices consume no rack units and are listed separately.",
    "No device is placed in a rack unit that another device already claims; the layout is checked for overlap."
  ],
